{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>What do you mean by all this camp that I met?</b> Now, Jacob's servants did as he commanded them, but he did not wish to receive it from them — or in his pride and wrath he did not speak with them and did not ask them 'Whose are you and where are you going,' and they feared approaching him. So now he said, 'What do you mean by all this camp,' for he thought that they belonged to Jacob by reason of the earlier angels, or those messengers had reported as much in Esau's camp, or there is not a single man on that road to account for it. And the meaning of 'What do you mean by all this camp' is: who is this to you that you should send him all these — that is, who is the great one with you to whom you would send all these? And he answered him, 'To find favor in the eyes of my lord,' for you are the great one and the lord in my eyes."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:53.262382011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}